def get_description(data: dict, short_code: str) -> str:
    for location in data["locations"]:
        if location.get("shortCode") == short_code:
            return location["description"]
    raise KeyError(f"No location with short code {short_code}")

This function is one way you can do this. It will raise an error if no location has the shortcode, or if the location with that shortcode has no description. If you would prefer different behavior in those cases, the logic can be adjusted slightly as need be.
